Z||000006||Oreif||06-23-2000||02:39 AM||||First, I E-mailed the guy and he says the vehicle was THE pace car for the middle part of the race. Second I looked in the "HP Book"<BR>"Fiero" by Gary Witzenburg and There are only 3 SD4 pace cars. There were 140 Pace cars as a promo at the race. They were all identical right down to the door decals and the Indy logo on the front fender (missing from the one on Yahoo) and red lugnuts.<BR>As for the location of the 3, One is in the Indy museum, One is at the GM corporate Museum, and the last one is at the Pontiac-Oakland Museum. (this is per the book, which was printed in 1987. It doesn't even list any 88 models)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||06-23-2000||09:41 AM||||I haven't been to the IMS Museum since 1998, but I know they didn't have the Fiero pace car on display then (though they did have a 1/24 scale model of it).  I wonder if the real car is sitting under a tarp in the IMS garages somewhere?<P>Maybe this fall, after the USGP, when things calm down around the IMS offices, I'll write their PR director and their historian to ask about the Fiero and see if they'd let a bunch of us come look at it.  Now that would be a fun and inexpensive get-together!||||reg||1
